---
title: Textarea
---

p.govuk-body
  | Textareas allow users to enter text that’s longer than a single line.

p.govuk-body
  | Users can find open-ended questions difficult to answer. It might be better
    to break up one complex question into a series of simple ones.

== render('/partials/example.*',
  caption: 'Generating a textarea with a label, hint and nine rows',
  code: text_area_with_label_and_hint_and_nine_rows)

== render('/partials/example.*',
  caption: 'Generating a textarea with a word limit',
  code: text_area_with_max_words) do

  p.govuk-body
    markdown:
      If a limit on the number of characters a user can enter is required, the
      `max_length` parameter can be used. Feedback on how close the user is to
      the limit will be shown benath the textarea. An error will be shown if
      the limit is exceeeded.

      To limit the number of words instead of characters also pass in `count_type: :words`

== render('/partials/example.*',
  caption: 'Generating a textarea with a character limit and threshold',
  code: text_area_with_max_chars_and_threshold) do

  p.govuk-body
    | If the limit is much higher than most users are likely to reach, you can
      choose to only display the message after a user has entered a certain
      amount.

  p.govuk-body
    | To do this, set the <code>threshold</code> parameter in conjunction with a
      word or character limit.

== render('/partials/example.*',
  caption: 'Customising the limit text',
  code: text_area_with_custom_limit_text) do

  markdown:
    When localising the textarea you can configure the strings used by the component using
    the parameters:

  ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
    li
      code under_limit_other_text
    li
      code under_limit_one_text
    li
      code at_limit_text
    li
      code over_limit_other_text
    li
      code over_limit_one_text

  markdown:
    The `%{count}` placeholder will be replaced by the number of characters or
    words away from the limit you are.

